The inconsistent scaling of lambda0 in my previous example seems to be due to bad automatic "usage" attributes with the default settings of reduce.capthist (it drops occasions with no detections, which is not what we want). Better with
CH7 <- reduce(CH1, by = 7, dropunused = FALSE)
CH14 <- reduce(CH1, by = 14, dropunused = FALSE)
...

# $fit7
# link estimate SE.estimate      lcl     ucl

# D        log  9.90146    1.888970  6.83532 14.3430
# lambda0  log  0.00241    0.000498  0.00161  0.0036

# sigma    log 20.87249    1.913922 17.44560 24.9725

#
# $fit14
# link estimate SE.estimate      lcl     ucl

# D        log  9.90145    1.888969  6.83531 14.3430

# lambda0  log  0.00241    0.000498  0.00161  0.0036

# sigma    log 20.87251    1.913928 17.44561 24.9726

